rs but in reality they are simply  massive suits of power armor inhabited  and controlled by small colonies of golo  mckee takes over the unsc gladius with a  swarm of unarmored legolo who quickly  overwhelm all human forces stationed on  the spacecraft before she boards however  there is a brief shot of a proper hunter  from behind only one leg and part of its  weaponized arm are visible but the shot  effectively sets up the arrival of the  hunters into the live-action halo world  though mckee makes short work of the  unsc gladius crew she isn't quite quick  enough to stop the ship's captain from  wiping all sensitive records from the  computer system just before she kills  him with her tiny energy fingernail he  tells the ship to activate the coal  protocol a phrase any fan of the halo  novels will be familiar with as it's the  title of one of the series most famous  books the cold protocol named for unsc  admiral preston coal is a directive  meant to keep the location of earth and  all related information out of the hands  of the covenant by invoking it before  his death the captain of the gladius  blocks mckee from accessing any truly  sensitive data from the ship the show  even goes so far as to include the cold  protocol's exact ordinance number on the  gladius computer screen emergency  priority order 09831a-1  it's a fun little detail that shows just  how much the series writers have paid  attention to the source material  the halo show is clear from the get-go  that the unsc is an authoritarian  military power which dips dangerously  close to outright fascism on many  occasions the organization's higher-ups  have no qualms about killing innocents  abducting children or conducting all  other manner of reprehensible deeds in  the name of order and dominance the unsc  facilities on reach include several  phrases plastered around the walls that  reflect humanity's military-centric  society some of which were pulled  directly from previous halo media one  such phrase appears behind dr halsey  while she's conducting experiments on  the forerunner keystone the phrase  together we prevail these words are part  of a famous poem in the original halo  canon called forward unto dawn which is  also the namesake of a unsc ship in halo  3.  last but not least forward unto dawn is  also the name of the live-action  mini-series produced during the lead-up  to the release of halo 4. another  reference to prior halo media and the  reach facilities appears in the silver  team barracks the phrase paramare  periteris perconstallatum translated it  reads by sea by land by the stars in the  original canon this is one of the chief  mottos of the unsc  the third episode of halo references a  number of locations from the original  series two of these illusions come in a  scene on the rubble in which sauron's  son shows kwan the gas giant hessian and  its smaller moon metaset  but no one goes there  i don't think there's any air  both of these celestial bodies are tied  to the rubble in the halo novels where  metaset's inhospitable atmosphere ends  up causing some serious problems for  humanity a covenant faction uses the  atmospheric conditions of the moon to  quickly grow an attack force of grunts  at the end of episode 3 there's also a  major reference to the planet eridanus 2  master chief's home world i saw it as a  child  on a writtenness too  this is consistent with the lore of the  games and the novels but the nature of  the planet seems to have been changed  significantly originally eridanus 2 was  a thriving and heavily populated world  with several major urban centers in the  show it's changed to be a colony world  wiped clean of human habitation by a  deadly plague  the halo show explores one of the darker  aspects of the franchise's lore how most  of the candidates for the unsc spartan 2  program were kidnapped as children on dr  halsey's orders after interacting with  the forerunner keystone master chief  begins to have flashbacks 